// SR 641.711 — Chapter 2 Technical Measures for Reducing Carbon Emissions from Buildings
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 16 Reporting
1 The cantons regularly report to the FOEN on technical measures for reducing carbon emissions from buildings.
2 The report must contain information regarding:
a. the CO2 measures taken and planned and their effectiveness; and
b. the progression of carbon emissions from buildings within the canton.
3 On request, the cantons shall make available to the FOEN all necessary documents that form the basis of the report.
|

:NOTE
Art. 16 — Inserted by No I of the O of 2 April 2025, in force since 1 May 2025 (AS 2025 248).
|

:INFO
Art. 16a Information on heat generation systems
In accordance with Article 9 paragraph 3 of the CO2 Act, the essential information on heat generation systems for heating and hot water in new buildings and for their replacements in old buildings is as follows:
a. the energy source used for the heat generation system;
b. the nominal output of the heat generation system or the district heating connection;
c. the heating requirement (Qh);
d. the year in which the heat generation system was commissioned;
e. the date of entry in the Federal Register of Buildings and Dwellings;
f. in the case of district heating: the Federal Building Identifier (EGID) for the building in which the main heat generation system or heat supplier is located.
|

:NOTE
Art. 16a — Inserted by No I of the O of 2 April 2025, in force since 1 May 2025 (AS 2025 248).

